            <h3>IT Infrastructure Intern</h3>
            <p>Associação GigaCandanga · Mar 2026 – present · Brasília, Brazil · hybrid</p>
          </header>
          <p>GigaCandanga is a Science and Technology Institution (ICT) responsible for managing Redecomep, the metropolitan education and research network of Brazil's Federal District.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Conducted proof-of-concept (PoC) implementations in a lab environment with Wazuh (SIEM), Suricata (IDS/IPS), and OpenVAS (vulnerability management) for Linux server security monitoring, with production rollout planned for future project phases.</li>
            <li>Configured and validated JumpServer (PAM) as a Bastion Host in a test environment, centralizing SSH access to Linux servers, enabling session auditing, and reducing direct credential exposure.</li>
            <li>Administered Linux systems and operated Zabbix and Grafana for high-capacity network observability.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Wazuh · Suricata · OpenVAS · Docker · Docker Compose · Linux · JumpServer · Zabbix · Grafana · TCP/IP · DNS · Firewall · Python</p>
